<task base="Anywhere" id="t00233">
	<title>Stowing the rear seat belt</title>
	<shortdesc>The rear seat belt buckles can be stowed in the pocket between the rear seatback and cushion when not in use.</shortdesc>
	<taskbody>
		<context>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01462">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01463">
									<image href="images/N_SP327_B06_019.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
		</context>
		<steps>
			<step>
				<cmd>Insert the seat belt metal tab into the two holes located on both sides. This will help keep the belts from being trapped behind or under the seats.</cmd>
				<info>
					<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01464">
						<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
							<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
							<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
							<tbody>
								<row rowsep="1">
									<entry colname="col1">
										<fig id="e01465">
											<image href="images/N_SP327_C06_025_1_ER.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
										</fig>
									</entry>
									<entry colname="col2"/>
								</row>
							</tbody>
						</tgroup>
					</table></info>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>After inserting the seat belt, tighten the belt webbing by pulling it up.</cmd>
				<info>
					<note type="tip">
						<p>When pulling out the seat belt to wear it, slowly pull the tab out of the seat belt guide so that the guide does not come off the trim.</p>
					</note>
				</info>
			</step>
		</steps>
	</taskbody>
	<related-links>
